{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"ETF creation/redemption charges are fund-level amounts intended to offset costs the fund incurs processing an order. **Fixed fees** generally cover routine processing/administrative costs; **variable fees** (often called transaction or cash-in-lieu fees) cover estimated trading, market-impact, and other costs of acquiring or disposing of portfolio holdings, including cash substitutions. The authorized participant (AP) placing the order typically pays the fund; these charges help protect existing shareholders from dilution. The fund’s board or disclosed procedures set them, and amounts may differ by fund and order.\n\nSeparately, an AP may charge its client (for example, an ETF market maker) compensation for its own services, hedging, financing, and operational costs. That is not a fund charge. **Recipients can differ:** fund fees go to the fund (or, under its arrangements, a service provider), while AP compensation goes to the AP."}}
